all right in all seriousness everyone  keeps asking uh  why  are we shutting the show down there's  basically three reasons right  the first is uh when we started this  show i committed to myself uh that i was  gonna do it for at least one year one  year i was going to do it  and a huge decision that i made last  year  was that i returned all uninvested  outside capital uh on the investing  business and i basically just said look  i don't give a [ __ ] about uh kind of  doing what other people want me to do  i'm going to do what i want to do  and it turned out to be a fantastic  decision  at the time i considered  to go ahead and stop doing the show as  well  but i committed to myself i was gonna do  it for one year and i felt that uh that  was important to keep uh keep doing  the second thing  is that there's a lot of folks who  complain  about the news the media the mainstream  media uh they like to point fingers and  say these people are idiots these people  don't understand what's going on in the  world  these people have no clue how to  communicate all that stuff  there's not very many people  who can now say that for a year  they built something similar  ran it and saw inside the belly of the  beast  the incentives are so [ __ ] up  it is so screwed up  the incentives go towards  clicks views all this type of stuff  it also a huge piece of it every single  person you see on twitter that's not  them every person you see on youtube for  the most part that's not them every  person that you end up watching on  somewhere on the internet that's not  them they become characters of  themselves  and for me i'm just not interested in it  i really don't care about the day-to-day  news stuff  i don't really  find a lot of uh kind of the the  tertiary conversations or  kind of the the everyday events super  interesting um and what the incentives  end up doing is they not only pull you  into a lot of nonsense but on top of  that uh it also takes somebody like  myself who my number one goal in life is  to learn and to just spend as much time  as i possibly can learning uh and it  pulls you out of the student role and it  puts you into the teacher role and  there's value to that and i talk to  people every single day who watch this  show  and what ends up occurring is uh they've  learned something they've got some value  out of the show and i appreciate that  and i'm glad that that's happened  but i don't want to be the teacher i  don't think that i've got all of the  information i don't want to be the  person who's looked at for the answers  instead i want to be  in the student role i want to be the one  who gets to ask the questions who gets  to learn who gets to seek out the most  interesting people the people who have  information i don't have and uh and go  and learn and so uh in some ways the  incentives and it's not just this show  it's not just mainstream media it's  every single other person in the bitcoin  community every single other person in  the crypto community and every single  other person in any other industry that  does something that is a daily show the  incentives are screwed up and they will  end up in the same place  it's because the incentives are off and  so naturally  me  shutting this down is me saying i'm not  gonna play that game right it's the  wrong game to play and i don't like  playing this game and so  if you can't change the incentives then  go do something else since that's what  we're doing here  and i think that naturally where you see  trust across society is people are not  trusting the mainstream media they're  not trusting news sources instead what  they're doing is they're going towards  longer form conversations like i have  done for years  and they're going towards people uh that  they get to know over time and so uh  we've been doing this now for i don't  know four years almost five years and so  that's what we're going to spend most of  our time doing is we're going to double  and triple down on the long form  conversations uh probably many of you  that's how you originally  found some of the content found myself  or found what we were talking about  and then lastly  is as many of you know  plain and i had a a daughter she's uh  eight months old and this is a huge time  commitment to do this every single day  uh we spend anywhere just on the  recordings two and a half to three hours  a day and that's just for the live video  most people don't realize there is  nobody make no doubt there is nobody in  the world who can keep up with me when  it comes to output  every single day for over a year  we have produced a written newsletter  that i write myself  two podcast episodes five youtube videos  a two-hour live stream and all the  social content and obviously the rest of  the team is incredibly helpful in terms  of uh producing that stuff editing it  all that type of stuff  but we don't get to create that content  unless i sit here and i record or i  write or i tweet or i post it and so  naturally that time commitment uh it's  fun i enjoy doing some of it but i want  to spend more time with pelina and i  want to spend more time with our  daughter and so when you kind of add all  that up between  an aspect of uh the incentives are off i  want to be the student not the teacher  and i want to  be more in control of my time i want to  be able to do what i want to do when i  want to do it i don't want to have to  say to a friend who says hey do you want  to come to this event do you want to  come do this thing hey do you want to  grab lunch oh sorry i can't do that  right and so naturally those three  things led to me saying to myself hey  let's shut down the live show and what  we're going to do is we're going to  still create tons of content you're  going to see  lots and lots of long form interviews  hour hour and a half two hours some of  them we've already recorded some of them  we have planned over the next couple of  weeks you're going to still see tons of  writing tweets videos all that type of  stuff but at the end of the day uh i  think that each one of you are watching  this if there's one thing i ask that you  take away from all this is just ask  yourself every day when you wake up do  you do the [ __ ] that you want to do or  do you do the [ __ ] that you think you're  supposed to do  and over time if you can keep doing more  and more the [ __ ] that you want to do  you live a much happier life and so  with that  i love you all  we will still post a [ __ ] ton of content  i hope that you continue to learn the  number one thing that you can do for us  watch the content share with your  friends  we will continue to do our best  i hope that you guys enjoy it  i love you  see you  you
 

